      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community began in 1902 as a planned stop on the Dayton–Greenville interurban traction line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fort_mckinley_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area was once called Poor Hook before being formally platted in 1905, sparking residential growth tied to the traction network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fort_mckinley_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "McKinley Branch Library, built in 1955, reflects post‑World War II expansion in the Dayton Metro Library system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
